# Victoria Metrics Server Configuration Template
# This template configures the command-line arguments for the Victoria Metrics server.
# It is designed to be self-documenting and safe for reuse within an Ansible role.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Storage Configuration
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# storage_data_path: The path to the directory where Victoria Metrics stores its data.
# Default: /var/lib/victoria-metrics
#
# The -storageDataPath argument tells the Victoria Metrics server where to persist
# its time-series data on disk. Ensure this directory exists and has sufficient
# permissions for the Victoria Metrics process to read and write.

# Construct the ARGS string safely.
# We use a Jinja raw block to prevent Jinja from interpreting the literal
# double curly braces in the command-line argument syntax if the variable
# values were to contain them (though unlikely for paths), and to ensure
# the output format `-storageDataPath=<value>` is preserved exactly.
# However, since the value itself is a simple string path, standard interpolation
# is sufficient and safer for escaping. We wrap it in quotes to handle spaces in paths.

{% set _storage_data_path = storage_data_path | default('/var/lib/victoria-metrics') %}

# Command-line arguments passed to the Victoria Metrics server.
# These arguments control the runtime behavior and configuration of the server.
# When running under systemd, special care must be taken with shell escaping
# for regexes (double backslashes) and newlines.
ARGS="-storageDataPath={{ _storage_data_path | quote }}"
